with it.

4.1 VENDORED CODE

    audiobook-studio/tools/vendor/

    Each vendored project carries its own license and copyright holders; see the
    LICENSE file within each directory.

4.2 SPEECH CORPORA

Reference audio used to clone the narrator's voice, and legacy audition material
retained so earlier results stay reproducible. This is recorded audio of real
people from public research corpora. It is not the copyright holder's work and is
not offered under section 3.

Every item below is MODIFIED from its source: clips were selected and
concatenated, silences trimmed or compacted, levels normalised, and in some cases
excerpts spliced. Both licenses involved require that modification be stated, so
it is stated here and the per-file processing steps are recorded alongside the
audio in the accompanying .json and PROVENANCE.md files.

    audiobook-studio/assets/voice-refs/hifitts/

    Hi-Fi Multi-Speaker English TTS Dataset (Hi-Fi TTS), OpenSLR SLR109.
    https://openslr.org/109/
    Licensed CC BY 4.0 -- https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Built from public-domain LibriVox audiobooks and Project Gutenberg texts.

        Bakhturina, E., Lavrukhin, V., Ginsburg, B. and Zhang, Y.
        "Hi-Fi Multi-Speaker English TTS Dataset", 2021. arXiv:2104.01497

    This is the voice of the audiobook. Speaker 92, `clean` subset. Modified:
    selected clips concatenated to about 25 seconds and peak-normalised. See
    voice-refs/hifitts/PROVENANCE.md for the sha256, the exact selection, and an
    open question about speaker consent that the dataset's authors raise.

    audiobook-studio/assets/voice-refs/emns-refs/
    audiobook-studio/assets/provenance/qvoice-legacy/qvoice/frontier-british-female-*.wav

    Emotive Narrative Storytelling (EMNS) corpus, OpenSLR SLR136.
    https://openslr.org/136/
    Licensed Apache 2.0 -- https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

        Kari, N., Xiaosong, Y. and Jian, Z. "EMNS /Imz/ Corpus: An emotive
        single-speaker dataset for narrative storytelling in games, television
        and graphic novels", 2023.

    Rejected as the narrator's voice after the listener identified audible hiss.
    Retained as audition evidence. Modified: excerpts spliced with compacted
    gaps, edge-trimmed and RMS-normalised; the qvoice-legacy copies are further
    denoised. Steps recorded in the adjacent .json files.

    audiobook-studio/assets/voice-refs/common-voice-refs/

    Mozilla Common Voice, released under CC0 1.0 Universal.
    https://commonvoice.mozilla.org/

    Rejected as the narrator's voice for being too narrow in pitch range.
    Retained as audition evidence. Modified: trimmed and tightened. CC0 asks for
    no attribution; it is given for traceability rather than obligation. The
    specific corpus release and clip identifiers were not recorded at the time,
    which is a gap in this project's provenance rather than in the source.

A note on why these are kept at all: a voice reference is the one input that
cannot be regenerated from a seed. Deleting the rejected candidates would make
the audition record unverifiable, and deleting the chosen one would make the
audiobook's narrator irreproducible.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. RESERVATION OF RIGHTS, AND FUTURE WORKS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This section states the author's position. It does not enlarge or reduce any
permission granted above, and it is not legal advice.

NON-EXCLUSIVE, AND NOTHING IS TRANSFERRED

    The grants in sections 1 and 3 are non-exclusive licenses, not assignments.
    Copyright in the novel prose, the planning documents, the lyrics, the cover,
    and the recordings remains with Jessica Mulein, and with Mulein Studios LLC
    where named. All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

THE AUTHOR'S OWN USE IS NOT LIMITED

    Nothing above restricts the author. She may write sequels, prequels,
    adaptations, retellings, and further works in this world; may reuse any
    character, name, setting, structure, phrase, or passage; may produce works
    that overlap with or are substantially similar to this corpus; and may license
    any of it to anyone else on any terms, including terms that differ from those
    offered here. ShareAlike in section 1 binds those who receive the work, not
    the person who wrote it.

IDEAS ARE NOT OWNED; THIS WORLD IS LICENSED NON-COMMERCIALLY

    Copyright protects expression, not ideas. The premise, the technical conceits,
    the ethical argument and the questions this book asks are not owned by anyone.
    Others remain free to write about addressable thought and consent, and the
    author remains free to return to it.

    The Mindwars world is a different matter, and section 1 is deliberate about
    it. Characters, settings and the shape of a fictional world are protectable
    expression, and section 1 licenses adaptation. So anyone may build in this
    world -- new stories with Mara Venn, Nia Calder, Safiya Mir, the null, the
    Trust, the Radius -- provided they credit, do not use it commercially, and
    release what they build under the same terms.

    This is intended, not an oversight. It is also irrevocable for this version,
    as stated below.

    What NonCommercial reserves is the commercial lane. No one may sell a work
    built on this corpus. Sequels, adaptations, and continuations offered for sale
    remain the author's alone, and she needs no permission to build on her own
    book.

    NOTE FOR FUTURE WORK: material published in this repository is openly
    licensed, including everything under The Final Frontier Novel/planning/ --
    the canon bible, arc outline, decisions and ledgers. Worldbuilding intended
    for a commercially published sequel should therefore be developed outside this
    repository. Adding it here licenses it non-commercially to everyone, and that
    cannot be undone afterwards.

NO TRADEMARK LICENSE

    No section grants any right in a name, title, or mark, including "The Final
    Frontier", "Mindwars", "Mulein Studios", or "Digital Defiance". Any such
    rights, if they exist, are separate from copyright and are not licensed here.

    On the title: a title is not protected by copyright, so nothing here depends
    on one. "Space: the final frontier" is strongly associated with Star Trek,
    and any exposure that creates would be a trademark question about likelihood
    of confusion rather than a copyright one. This novel shares no characters,
    setting, or universe with that work; it is a story about neural privacy and
    consent, and the phrase predates its famous use as ordinary English.

WHAT THE AUTHOR CANNOT TAKE BACK

    Stated plainly because it is the one real limit. A Creative Commons 4.0
    license is irrevocable for material already distributed under it. Later
    versions of this work may carry different terms, and distribution here may
    stop at any time, but anyone who has already received this corpus under
    CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 keeps those permissions permanently. Relicensing changes the
    future, not the past.

CONTRIBUTIONS

    Because a contributor holds copyright in what they write, accepted
    contributions could otherwise constrain the author's ability to relicense or
    to reuse this material in later works. CONTRIBUTING.md states the terms on
    which contributions are accepted so that does not happen.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. A NOTE ON AI CONTRIBUTION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The prose in this novel was drafted by AI systems against specifications,
outlines, and editorial decisions written by Jessica Mulein, then revised under
her direction. The song lyrics are written by Jessica Mulein; their composition
and performance are AI-produced. Copyright is claimed in the human authorship:
the selection, arrangement, direction, and revision that produced these works.

This note is disclosure, not a term of license. It does not enlarge or reduce
any permission granted above.
